# TODO: Verification Plan for Polynomial Encoding Functions

## Overview

This document describes the TODO plan for verifying the functions and constants
listed in [`doc/truong/poly_functions.txt`](../truong/poly_functions.txt), which
enumerates all fully qualified function and constant names from
`src/encoding/polynomial.rs` (Rust source). These are extracted into
`Spqr/Code/Funs.lean` (Lean 4 / Aeneas extraction).

All extractable functions are configured via
[`aeneas-config.yml`](../../aeneas-config.yml). Functions not appearing in
that configuration (e.g. `#[cfg(test)]` or `#[cfg(feature = "test-utils")]`
items) are not extracted and therefore cannot be verified in the current
framework.

The current Lean specification tree for the polynomial layer lives at
[`Spqr/Specs/Encoding/Polynomial/`](../../Spqr/Specs/Encoding/Polynomial/)
and is grounded mathematically by
[`Spqr/Math/Poly.lean`](../../Spqr/Math/Poly.lean) (with helpers in
[`Spqr/Math/Poly/`](../../Spqr/Math/Poly/)).

